@baseUrl = http://localhost:4001

### 1. Create a product to archive (setup, expect 201)
# @name toArchive
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Archive Test",
  "barcode": "archive-001",
  "priceInCentavos": 1000,
  "stock": 5
}

### 2. DELETE (archive) it (expect 204, empty body)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{toArchive.response.body.$._id}}

### 3. GET it by id (expect 200, isActive false, proves it was archived, not deleted)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{toArchive.response.body.$._id}}

### 4. DELETE it again (expect 204, idempotent)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{toArchive.response.body.$._id}}

### 5. DELETE valid-format id that doesn't exist (expect 404, no "headers already sent" in terminal)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/products/507f1f77bcf86cd799439011

### 6. DELETE malformed id (expect 400)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/products/abc

### 7. GET all (the archived product should still be in the list)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products